  "id": "velkspreownedfurnishings",
  "neon": "#ff8a4a",
  "note": "VELK'S PRE-OWNED FURNISHINGS — the second-hand furniture warehouse on Ironside Street.\n\n⚠ THE HOIST IS THE WHOLE DESIGN. A furniture warehouse is a building you get a wardrobe OUT of, so\nwhat it needs is a loading door on the first floor, a beam over it and a shutter under it — and that\none arrangement says more about the trade than any amount of shopfront. The arm drew it as a junk\nshop with a window.\n\n⚠ THE BIG SIGN IS ON THE FLANK, NOT THE FRONT. A gable end is where a real city puts its largest\nadvertisement, because it is the one surface a wall texture cannot make interesting — and the front\nof this building is almost entirely door, so there is nowhere on it for a sign that size. That is\nwhat `face: 'x'` on a `bladePanel` is for.\n\n⚠ AND THE UPPER WINDOWS ARE FEW AND DIRTY. A warehouse is not an office: three small openings up a\nfour-storey wall, not a ribbon, and nothing behind them is lit.",
  "pal": "ty_signalbox",
  "replaces": "junkshop",
